# Variants

*Reference.*

{{humanName}} ships the following variants. Reference any icon as `{{packageName}}::<variant>/<icon-name>` (or just `<icon-name>` for the default variant).

| Variant | Path prefix | Style |
|---|---|---|
| `default` | `<name>` (no prefix needed) | <!-- describe the default variant --> |
| <!-- add rows for additional variants --> | | |

## Examples

```blade
{{-- Default variant --}}
<x-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::home" class="w-6 h-6" />

{{-- Explicit variant path --}}
<x-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::default/home" class="w-6 h-6" />
```

Fluent helper:

```blade
{{ ichava('{{packageName}}::home')->color('#4338ca')->class('w-6 h-6') }}
```

## Variant enum (PHP)

```php
use {{namespace}}\Enums\Variant;

Variant::DEFAULT->value;            // 'default'
Variant::DEFAULT->isDefault();      // true
Variant::default();                 // Variant::DEFAULT
```

The enum implements `IconSetVariantInterface` from core, so it works wherever core's registry expects a variant.

